    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0730" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg660"/>

                <head>No. 411.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Morgan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 22,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 421.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 638, of the 4th instant, concerning the case of Captain Caleb, of the
                    Adriana, and to say that the Department duly appreciates the courtesy of Señor
                    Romero Rubio, whom you consulted with reference to certain proceedings
                    respecting the same.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
